From: gennro <gennro2004@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] scsi: ufs: qcom: don't enable the lane clocks twice

ufs_qcom_enable_lane_clks() prepares and enables every clock of the host
(devm_clk_bulk_get_all()), but only ufs_qcom_disable_lane_clks() checks
is_lane_clks_enabled. A runtime resume with the link in hibern8 enables
them twice: ufshcd_setup_clocks(on) -> ufs_qcom_setup_clocks(PRE_CHANGE)
and then ufs_qcom_resume(). The next suspend disables them once, so every
cycle leaks one reference on gcc_ufs_phy_axi_clk, unipro_core, ahb and
the symbol clocks (and 3x on bi_tcxo ref_clk on a Retroid Pocket 5).

Those clocks then never turn off, not even in system suspend: they keep
GPLL0 and the RPMh XO vote (bi_tcxo) on, so the SoC can't shut XO down
or reach AOSS sleep / CX collapse in s2idle.

Return early when the clocks are already enabled, mirroring the disable
side.

[ Holodor: from kettlelinux 40-kettle/1160 ]
---
--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
@@ -356,6 +356,16 @@ static int ufs_qcom_enable_lane_clks(struct ufs_qcom_host *host)
 {
 	int err;
 
+	/*
+	 * Called from ufs_qcom_setup_clocks(on) when the link is in hibern8 and
+	 * again from ufs_qcom_resume(): enabling twice while the disable side
+	 * runs once leaks one reference to every UFS clock (the bulk set is all
+	 * of them) per runtime resume, so they never turn off again, keep XO
+	 * voted on and block SoC sleep (AOSS, CX collapse).
+	 */
+	if (host->is_lane_clks_enabled)
+		return 0;
+
 	err = clk_bulk_prepare_enable(host->num_clks, host->clks);
 	if (err)
 		return err;
